r the past year (13 sales, net $103.0M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.8% (0.6% in buybacks and 0.4% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 20 consecutive years, raising it 34.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 22,700 employees, each generates about $401K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 15.3% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $45K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.4M (11x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":73,"head":"Watch: composite 58, above the 57 line, but no margin of safety and the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread); it becomes a buy below $830.","pros":["Composite 58, above the 57 line (gates 15/26)","ROIC 30.1% vs WACC 11.0%","FCF margin 11.3%","Revenue grew 26.1%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $836.7M"],"cons":["Trades 7% above fair value of $976","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","EV/EBITDA 16.3x vs sector 12.9x","P/FCF 35.4x vs sector 21.8x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)"],"buy_below":829.52,"vc":{"base":975.91,"base_src":"dcf","bear":411.39,"bull":2295.47,"alt_median":335.7,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.9071,"dispersion":0.5497,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (55% dispersion)","DCF is 191% above the other models' median ($336)","bull case is 5.6x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gross_margin":0.2864,"fcf_margin":0.0677,"div_yield":0.0151}},"mc_quantiles":[197.3,312.6,411.39,481.0,550.97,618.21,691.33,754.38,827.78,892.89,988.94,1069.83,1173.48,1261.99,1408.21,1543.63,1730.74,1953.1,2295.47,2896.38,4506.33],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.918,"discount_rate":0.048,"terminal_growth":0.002,"exit_multiple":0.032},"ticker":"FIX","date":"2026-11-20"}